/// Interface-spec vectors from MAINNET, captured 2026-09-24 by anonymous v3 requests to
/// icp-api.io (the capture script is in the moxzi repository, scripts/ic_agent_vectors/):
/// three query responses as the boundary node returned them -- the ICP ledger (root subnet,
/// no delegation), ckBTC (an application subnet, delegated) and an Internet Identity
/// REJECTION (delegated, with `error_code`) -- each with the `/subnet` read_state certificate
/// of the same canister. Every signature here was made by a real replica node; nothing is
/// synthetic, so a check that passes proves the agent computes what the IC signs.
///
/// Time checks are off (`now = null`) except where a check is ABOUT time: the vectors are
/// old by the time this runs, which is exactly what the #stale checks exercise.
///
/// Also: Candid effective-canister-id routing (vectors cross-checked with agent-js's IDL
/// decoder), tree well-formedness, `lookup*`, and the Ed25519 no-trap guard.
